g the lead from +4.3 to -3.2, and the engine's choice was B3. It was the worst move of Opus 5.5's game, and White's reply G6 then won back 7.4 points."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "C1 cost 6.2 points and turned a +2.3 lead into -3.9, with the engine preferring G8. The bottom-left corner was already filling with White stones, and this move did not help Black there."}, {"turn": 49, "text": "G4 lost 6.6 points and left Black at -18.8, the lowest of the game, with the engine's choice being J3. White's three captured stones of Black had given it a large lead, and this looked like the end of the game."}, {"turn": 50, "text": "The 16k played J3 and lost 22.8 points, the biggest swing of the game, taking the lead from -18.8 to +4.0 for Black. The engine's choice was H1, and with J3 taken the game went to Opus 5.5."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran works on the current position or on records: libs.py (shown) flood-fills groups and prints their liberties, the inline script counts stones plus enclosed empty regions as an area score, and the cat/tail and games.md append only read and write the game log. None of it enumerates candidate moves, scores them, or plays any continuation forward.", "stop": false}}